  'tshwane-overnight-restrictions-14-reservoirs-2026-10-27',
  'Tshwane widens overnight water cuts to 14 reservoirs',
  'Utilities', '2026-10-27', 'SAnews', 'https://www.sanews.gov.za/node/85236',
  'Tshwane Mayor Nasiphi Moya says the city has begun overnight water restrictions at 14 reservoirs to let depleted supplies recover.',
  'The City of Tshwane has started overnight restrictions at 14 reservoirs that still hold adequate storage but are being drained by very high consumption, Executive Mayor Nasiphi Moya said this week. The city has also set up a daily evening Water Management Committee of senior officials and technical teams to coordinate its response across the metro''s water systems.

Moya said the restrictions aim to take the strain off Rand Water''s bulk supply system and allow critically low reservoirs, including those serving Garsfontein and Klapperkop, a chance to refill, while acknowledging that more residents will face temporary inconvenience. She also addressed a social media video showing a major leak in Garsfontein, saying it was outdated footage from a pipe that crews fixed days earlier, and that no such leak remains there now.

Separately, the city said production has resumed at the Roodeplaat Water Treatment Plant after electrical repairs, which should help restore supply to the Montana system. Nine tankers have been assigned to deliver water to Ekangala, and a centralised point is being set up to coordinate tanker routes, while independent tanker operators must now be verified by the city and have their water tested before they can distribute it to residents.

Unsafe water advisories remain in force in Hammanskraal''s Phase 3 network and in Bronkhorstspruit, where Rand Water is leading rehabilitation work at the treatment plant. A boil-water advisory for the Pretoria CBD''s Findlay Reservoir, by contrast, was lifted on 24 October.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.sanews.gov.za/node/85236", "https://www.timeslive.co.za/news/south-africa/2026-10-27-tshwane-introduces-overnight-water-restrictions-at-14-reservoirs/"]',
  'agent'
);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news (
  slug, title, category, published_date, source_name, source_url,
  summary, body, image_url, image_credit, image_source, verification_json, source
) VALUES (
  'caf-super-cup-referee-dahane-beida-loftus-2026-10-21',
  'CAF names referee for Sundowns'' Super Cup final at Loftus',
  'Sport', '2026-10-21', 'CAF', 'https://www.cafonline.com/caf-super-cup/news/media-accreditation-window-officially-open-for-totalenergies-caf-super-cup-2026/',
  'CAF has appointed Mauritanian referee Dahane Beida for the 2026 Super Cup final between Sundowns and USM Alger at Loftus on 8 November.',
  'The Confederation of African Football has appointed Mauritanian referee Dahane Beida to take charge of the 2026 CAF Super Cup final, which brings Mamelodi Sundowns and Algeria''s USM Alger to Loftus Versfeld in Pretoria on Sunday, 8 November.

Sundowns qualify for the final as the reigning CAF Champions League winners, while USM Alger come into the match as holders of the CAF Confederation Cup. The Super Cup is an annual one-off match between the champions of Africa''s two continental club competitions.

CAF has also opened its media accreditation window for the final. Journalists wanting to cover the match from Loftus Versfeld had until Thursday, 29 October, to apply through the CAF Media Channel, with the confederation noting that accreditation is not granted on a first-come, first-served basis.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.cafonline.com/caf-super-cup/news/media-accreditation-window-officially-open-for-totalenergies-caf-super-cup-2026/", "https://en.africatopsports.com/caf-dahane-beida-appointed-referee-for-2026-caf-super-cup-final/"]',
  'agent'
);
